<poml>
  <meta>
    <id>extended_parity.plan.poml-go-sdk</id>
    <version>0.2.0</version>
    <owner>poml-go-sdk</owner>
  </meta>
  <role>Complete Extended POML support per upstream proposal with tests/goldens and docs.</role>

  <task caption="Segmentation & parsing">
    <list>
      <item>Mixed content: DONE via synthetic `<poml mode="extended">` wrapper + text fallback. NEXT: optional smarter segmentation of tag fragments inside text while preserving whitespace/comments.</item>
      <item>Text escape: DONE (`<text>` treated as literal, round-trips).</item>
      <item>Metadata anywhere: TODO — allow `<meta>` outside top; normalize into Document.Meta while preserving order/comments.</item>
      <item>Aliasing: TODO — load component aliases from upstream definitions if available; otherwise keep current short tags.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Validation rules">
    <list>
      <item>Extended vs default: PARTIAL — text blocks gated; unknowns allowed ExtendedOn. TODO: clearer errors for extended-only tags/media.</item>
      <item>Strict Extended: TODO — enforce required meta/role/task; validate extended media sizes/attrs; surface element/field in details.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Converters">
    <list>
      <item>Carry text blocks, ops/figures, unknowns through message_dict/dict/OpenAI/LangChain/scene formats in Extended mode (PARTIAL: text gated; ops/figures handled).</item>
      <item>Ensure default (ExtendedOff) omits extended content safely (PARTIAL: text gated; ops/figures conditional).</item>
      <item>TODO: add goldens for mixed-content conversions and extended media.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Fixtures & goldens">
    <list>
      <item>TODO: add mixed-content fixtures (text + tags), text-escape fixtures, extended media/object fixtures.</item>
      <item>TODO: goldens for Extended converts (OpenAI/LangChain/message_dict) and round-trip parse→encode.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Docs & CLI">
    <list>
      <item>TODO: document Extended opt-in (root mode="extended" or flags), supported tags, and limits.</item>
      <item>TODO: note defaults (Extended off, unknowns gated); include examples for text escape and mixed files.</item>
    </list>
  </task>

  <task caption="Acceptance criteria">
    <list>
      <item>All new fixtures pass go test ./poml/... and match goldens.</item>
      <item>Extended mode can parse mixed text/POML files and `<text>` escapes without losing content.</item>
      <item>Converters include extended nodes when enabled and exclude them when off, with goldens for mixed cases.</item>
      <item>README/CLI flags clearly describe Extended behavior.</item>
    </list>
  </task>
</poml>
